			<item>
				<title>kpack</title>
				<link>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/kpack/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/kpack/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/buildpacks-community/kpack&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;kpack&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a Kubernetes-native platform that uses unprivileged Kubernetes primitives to perform buildpacks builds and keep application images up-to-date.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/buildpacks-community/kpack&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;kpack&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is part of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/buildpacks-community&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Buildpacks Community&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; organization.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>CircleCI</title>
				<link>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/circleci/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/circleci/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://circleci.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;CircleCI&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a continuous integration and delivery platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The CNB project maintains an integration, called an &lt;a href=&#34;https://circleci.com/orbs/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;orb&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&#xA;which allows users to run &lt;a href=&#34;https://buildpacks.io/docs/install-pack&#34;&gt;pack&lt;/a&gt; commands inside their pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Gitlab Auto DevOps</title>
				<link>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/gitlab/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/gitlab/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://about.gitlab.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Gitlab&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a web-based DevOps platform. The &lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/topics/autodevops/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Auto DevOps&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; feature uses &lt;a href=&#34;https://buildpacks.io/docs/install-pack&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pack&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;to build applications prior to deploying them.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Project &#34;Piper&#34;</title>
				<link>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/piper/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/piper/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.project-piper.io/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Project &amp;ldquo;Piper&amp;rdquo;&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a set of ready-made continuous delivery pipelines for direct use in your project.&#xA;It now also implements the CNB Platform spec as a step and makes it available in your Jenkins pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.project-piper.io/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Project &amp;ldquo;Piper&amp;rdquo;&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is maintained by &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.sap.com/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;SAP&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Tekton</title>
				<link>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/tekton/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/how-to/integrate-ci/tekton/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://tekton.dev/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Tekton&lt;svg class=&#34;external-link-icon&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;1em&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 3 21 3 21 9&#34;&gt;&lt;/polyline&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;21&#34; y2=&#34;3&#34;&gt;&lt;/line&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;visually-hidden&#34;&gt;(opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is an open-source CI/CD system running on k8s.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The CNB project has created a reference &amp;ldquo;task&amp;rdquo; for performing buildpacks builds with or without extensions (aka Dockerfile to be applied) top&#xA;of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://buildpacks.io/docs/for-platform-operators/concepts/lifecycle&#34;&gt;lifecycle&lt;/a&gt; tool (i.e. they do not use &lt;code&gt;pack&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
	</channel>
